1 III. Voting and non-voting members of the commission shall serve until replaced by their
2 respective appointing authority, until no longer meeting the conditions on which their original
3 appointmentwasbased,oruntilresignation.
4 IV. Legislative members shall receive mileage at the legislative rate when attending to the
5 dutiesofthecommission.
6 V. The commission shall review charitable gaming laws, including historical horse race
7 gaming, shall consider the issues identified in the November 1, 2024, final report of the commission
8 tostudytheeffectofrecentchangesmadetocharitablegaminglaws,includingthenewlyauthorized
9 historical horse races established in 2023, 79:583, and shall make from time to time such
10 recommendationsforadministrativeandlegislativechangestocharitablegaminglawandrulesasit
11 deems necessary and appropriate. The commission may upon a majority vote of the commission
12 take-upanysuchtopicsitdeemsrelevant;however,itshallstartwithpriorityconsiderationof:
13 (a) Anypossiblechangesneededtoaddressproblemgambling.
14 (b) Any possible changes needed to restructure or modify systems for allocating and
15 overseeing the use of funds granted to the state and to charities and gaming operators participating
16 ingamesofchanceandinhistoricalhorseracegaming.
17 (c) Any possible changes needed to prevent undue concentration or proliferation of
18 gaming locations, facilities, and ownership, including a municipal option to opt into or out of
19 componentsofcharitablegaming.
20 VI. The voting members of the study commission shall elect a chairperson from among the
21 voting members. The first meeting of the commission shall be called by the first-named house
22 member. The first meeting of the commission shall be held within 60 days of the effective date of
23 thissection. Fourvotingmembersofthecommissionshallconstituteaquorum.
24 VII. The commission shall submit a report on or before November 1, 2026, and on or before
25 September 1 of each year thereafter, to the general court including findings, recommendations, and
26 anycorrectiveortechnicalimprovementsthatcharitablegamingmayrequire.
27 VIII. Thecommissionshallbeadministrativelyattachedtothelotterycommission.
